{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791055043,"nonce":"zG3K8QdZW/PaV2mZTCohz3F+RS4=","title":"Hot reload refuses edits that shift the global table; remap globals instead","message":"An edit that adds a string literal (or a static) and removes another keeps\nthe globals count but shifts every global between them. Tailwind class edits\nin ashui do this routinely: ashui's classes2.hl edit (two class attributes)\nmoves 339 of 976 globals, e.g. g95 $Math \u003c-\u003e a String constant. Since\n9486007's fix such a reload is refused (\"globals moved: global N held X and\nholds Y\"); before it, the reload wrote the new constants over live globals and\ncrashed.\n\nTo apply these edits in place, a reload would map each new global to the old\nslot holding the same thing (a class descriptor by type, a static by owner and\nname, a constant by content), carry live values across, and either keep the\nrunning slot numbering for the new program or send every body that reads a\nmoved global back to the interpreter. Type descriptors' global_value pointers\ninto globals_data have to follow.\n\nReproducer: before2.hl and classes2.hl in ~/.cache/ashui-nuc/reload-clean on\nthe NUC (steps in 9486007).","files":null}]}